# ShannonBase Agent: tool-contract self-check.
#
# The agent's tools used to be described in six independent places -- the
# execute_tool() if-chain, the validate_tool_call() switch, the ML_WRITE_TOOLS
# approval table, ml_display_sql(), and two hand-written bilingual tool
# catalogues inside build_system_prompt() -- with nothing keeping them in
# sync, and mysql-test had no coverage of agent behaviour at all. They are now
# derived from one registry, and this test is what keeps them derived: it
# fails the moment a tool exists without a handler, without bilingual docs,
# with incoherent policy metadata, or missing from the generated prompt, and
# the moment validate_tool_call() stops producing the expected message for a
# fixed set of malformed calls.
#
# Needs no LLM and reads no user data.

--echo #
--echo # Tool registry / validation / prompt-catalogue contract
--echo #

# One row, 'OK'. Any other output names the tool and the contract it broke.
CALL sys.shannon_agent_selfcheck('tools', NULL, NULL);

--echo #
--echo # An unrecognised self-check kind is reported, not silently ignored
--echo #
CALL sys.shannon_agent_selfcheck('no_such_kind', NULL, NULL);
